    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and the full suite is green.\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`:\n\n- **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (new function step) \u2014 counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitive, trimmed) and throws a checked `OwnerCityCapacityException` when the count is already \u2265 50. It runs after the validate/telephone/household checks and before `BuildOwner`, so the still-unsaved owner isn't counted against itself.\n- **`OwnerCityCapacityException`** \u2014 checked exception carrying the city and count.\n- **`OwnerCityCapacityExceptionHandler`** + escalation YAML \u2014 responds **409** with `{\"errors\":[\"city\"]}`, mirroring the existing household-duplicate handler.\n- Wired the new `checkCityCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` (under `transaction` governance, consistent with the surrounding steps).\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fill a city to 50, 51st rejected) passes, and the full suite is green.",
